WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:05.400
<i>The Gourmet Festival
was supposed to be a fun holiday event.</i>

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:04.900
MAY 17, 2021

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:11.150
<i>Why couldn't Hazard Cast
predict the sudden tornado?</i>

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.120
<i>This giant thing came roaring in from the sea,
and all I could do was try to escape.</i>

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.120
GOURMET FESTIVAL HOST
MR. KODA-GEN

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.530
ABNORMAL WEATHER AT FAULT? TRUTH STILL UNKNOWN

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.040
<i>The catastrophe left 12 casualties
and 36 wounded.</i>

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:26.920
TRAGEDY AT GOURMET FESTIVAL: MEMORIAL SERVICES OF VICTIMS BEGIN

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.210
<i>It has been three days since the disaster,</i>

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:26.920
<i>and the memorial services
for the Gourmet Festival victims have begun.</i>

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.420
SERVICES FOR THE LATE
MR. HIROKI SHIRAKABA,
EXECUTIVE COMMITTEE MEMBER

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:37.550
SUNDAY NEWS

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:33.170
<i>Many people have gathered at the funeral hall
located in Shiotsuki, 24th Ward.</i>

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.550
<i>After the memorial services, we interviewed
Mayor Suido who was in attendance.</i>

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.430
<i>- Mayor Suido!
- Can we have a word about this tragedy?</i>

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.390
<i>There's a comment that the Hazard Cast warning
was delayed. Is that true?</i>

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.730
<i>It's simply due to the lack of cumulative data.</i>

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.530
<i>We will be taking measures so we can gather
even more data in the future.</i>

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.820
<i>What about the case of every network
within 24th Ward getting hacked?</i>

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.530
<i>My name is Carneades.</i>

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.370
<i>I am the one who will thrust choices
upon the world for the future.</i>

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.870
<i>It's been several days from that shocking hack,</i>

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.460
<i>but there has been no further statement
from the culprit.</i>

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:13.630
<i>Most people believe that it was a prank
by an overseas hacker group.</i>

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:19.550
<i>There are some occult rumors
saying that Carneades caused the tornado.</i>

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:22.930
One of the DoRed crew
found these this morning.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.980
They were at the Nijimi Station turnstile
and at the foot of Peace Bridge.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.230
That mark we saw from the hospital TV?

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:31.190
Yeah. I guess this was that guy's tag.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.480
I wonder if he's a street artist?

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.240
Before you think about that,
look at where the tagging happened.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.820
That's the thing.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.450
Both of them were in the locations
where we saw the Visions.

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.950
Yeah. This guy knows about
those trolley dilemmas.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.420
Moreover, if we're to believe his declaration,
the dilemmas were prepared by...

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.750
- You mean...
- That's enough.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.340
Shu.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.210
It's our fault.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.210
If we were able to handle the situation better...

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:01.300
No, if we didn't get carried away and involve
ourselves, someone else would of done a better—

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.220
There is nobody else.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.230
These dilemmas aren't given to anyone
other than us, yeah?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.810
We just have to start poking around
from what we know.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.770
Right.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.940
So both of you, let's meet up
if we get a call from Asumin.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.190
That's fine with me.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.030
Yeah.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.460
AUGUST 5, 2021

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.630
Koki is so enthusiastic.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.130
Interns don't usually work in this manner.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.220
He sure doesn't seem like
the distinguished son of the Suido family.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.760
That's true.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.890
<i>It's been three months.</i>

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:14.440
<i>We have no idea who that was,
and no phone calls from Asumi either.</i>

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.560
Good work today.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.310
Mr. Chikushi.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.280
Here's what you asked for.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.570
This helps a lot.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.400
This is all I can access
with my authorization level.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.820
No, I'm sorry for being so selfish.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:29.030
Are you hitting the Carneades case
from the Hazard Cast front?

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:29.790
Yes.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.210
Information about Hazard Cast
is top secret even within the SARG.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.040
But if you use your father's name...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.630
I can't do that. He hates nepotism.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:45.090
Right. You usually want to ask
disclosure of information in secret.

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.680
Well in that case,
you need some experience, yeah?

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.640
Since you're working so hard,
I'll toss you a special case.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.400
This is the thing that's starting
to get popular around Shantytown?

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:02.070
Yep. We want to do something about it
before it gets out of control.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.490
Why don't you try working on it
with Hana's group?

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:08.530
THE THREAT OF DRUG "D"
CONTINUOUSLY HARMING THE YOUTH

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:07.360
<i>Drug "D."</i>

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:12.240
In the past month,
we've been using the media to highly publicize

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.160
the sudden increase
of crime rates in Shantytown.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:20.090
I'm sure we'll start hearing a strong request
for redevelopment from the ward citizens.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.670
Mr. Howard, the Casino King.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:27.220
If we can build a casino in the 24th Ward,
we will succeed in building a casino in Japan

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.260
as soon as we're incorporated into Tokyo.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.430
Then let's move the project to the next phase.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:40.770
As promised, you will let me handle
the cleaning up and fundraising.

00:05:43.190 --> 00:05:45.530
<i>I am much obliged to you, Mr. Howard.</i>

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.910
Did you get the goods arranged?

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.080
<i>I will personally bring it to you
aboard the WINNER'S.</i>

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.700
Don't let me down.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.160
<i>I will promise results
that will be fitting for the cost.</i>

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.590
The vape... Where's the vape?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.170
If I don't have it... If I don't have it...

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:05.170
<i>Lucky, how are you doing?</i>

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.420
<i>Hold on a second!</i>

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.470
He's kinda thrashing around a lot.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.390
The withdrawal symptoms
for Drug D are ridiculous!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.890
There, it's open!

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:21.980
Yamamori, very good!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.730
That was a piece of cake for you!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.150
He got back up.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.280
- Vape! Give it to me!
- You bastard!

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.950
All right. How's that?

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.250
Ran, this is looking bad!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.000
- Hey there, move aside!
- Whoa!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.920
You're kidding me!

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.550
He's in no condition to be questioned.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.390
When will he come back to sanity?

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.060
Not for a while?

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:58.810
I don't see anything that look like drugs here.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.690
No pills, no powders,
no plants, no liquids. Nothing.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.110
A mysterious drug, huh?

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.820
Ran!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:09.780
Damn it, it's the SARG.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.780
Let's retreat before we bump into them.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:15.160
Why don't we just take that junkie with us?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.200
No. We can't afford to fail this case.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.080
<i>Drug D.
It spread too fast in such a short time.</i>

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.080
You have to avenge your nephew, of course.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.630
Well, you know how it goes.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.500
<i>I feel like someone's pulling the strings
in the background.</i>

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.210
I will never forgive that drug.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:29.880
Hey, Ran.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:32.300
Where are you going?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.640
Huh? The elevator moves?

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:36.890
When was it fixed?

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.520
Sometime this month.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.190
After so long?
Someone's quite whimsical, I see.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:46.440
Kunai's grandma has a bad leg,
so it helps her out a ton.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.900
Come to think of it,
I haven't seen Kunai in a while.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.030
Apparently he's been developing
some kind of new app.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.490
I get a reply once in a while.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.120
He's always been the type who doesn't come out
for a while once he shuts himself in.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.260
I'm heading out.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.100
Oh? Be safe, then.
Make sure to come back before it gets too late.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.310
Yeah. I'll see you.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.230
Shuta, get ready to close shop!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.940
Yeah, yeah.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.350
Hey, Mari. You're closing too?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:28.730
Yeah. Mom's stepping out,
so we're closing shop for today.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.980
I see.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.740
Is that Kozue?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.110
Yeah, that's Kozue.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.740
That's right, I heard
that she's been going out at night lately.

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:39.990
From who?

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.710
Mr. Shirakaba's wife.
I bumped into her the other day.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:49.090
How was Mrs. Kaba doing?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.970
She lost a lot of weight,
but it looked like she was doing her best.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.720
I see.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.550
Well, I'm a bit worried
so I'm gonna go after her.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:58.970
Wait!

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.220
It's dangerous for you, too.

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:02.560
Huh? But...

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.900
Then Shu, you can go instead of me.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.820
Fine, I'll go.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.400
Kozue!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:16.200
Where are you going?

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.660
It's dangerous to be by yourself.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:21.990
You're right. A suspicious person
is talking to me as we speak.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.250
Huh? Me?

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.000
I'll scream.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.790
I'm worried about you.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.000
- If you want to go somewhere, I'll come with—
- Leave me alone!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.170
Oh, hey!

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.840
Sheesh, there's no way I can do that.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.550
Hey, Kozue.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:41.810
I said I'd tag along, but this place is bad news.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.140
Kozue, this is no place
for kids to be wandering around.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.860
Kozue! Shantytown is no joke!

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:54.110
Then you can go home, Big Brother Shu.
I have something to do here.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.400
Something to do?
Do you have to do it right now?

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.740
Hey mister, wanna come play?

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.030
Oh, no thank you.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:03.370
- Don't call out to a guy with a kid.
- Oh, that reminds me.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.040
Want some rusk?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.410
What?

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.370
You liked rusks, didn't you?

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.630
I'm not a kid anymore,
so why are you baiting me with food?

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:15.710
What's wrong with you?

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.880
You've been stalking me.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:19.590
Well, you know...

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.600
Is this your atonement?

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.850
No, that's not what I meant it to be.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.310
You didn't have to save me.

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:35.070
Kozue, wh-what did you just...

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:38.610
- I should have died in his place!
- Oh, hey, Kozue!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.660
Hey Kozue, wait up!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.830
Huh, where did she go?

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:46.660
Damn it.

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.920
- H-Hey, are you all right?
- Excuse me!

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.300
You over there!

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:59.130
- Please keep that guy pinned down!
- Senpai, you shouldn't ask a civilian!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.590
You're Shuta Aoi!

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.890
She's from SARG.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.140
Don't let him get away! He's a drug dealer!

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:12.230
Oh, damn it!

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:13.770
Why do I have to do this?

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.240
Hey, get back here!

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.370
Outta my way!

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.330
- Is that you, Shuta?
- Koki?

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:34.170
Why are you chasing after him?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.460
Well, that's how things ended up.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:39.050
The scary SARG lady told me to.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.380
That guy is a drug dealer, right?

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.720
Yeah.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.890
The mysterious Drug D.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.100
Drug D?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.600
It's a drug that's highly addictive.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:54.520
It's still a mystery, but its users lose
their sense of judgment and become violent.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:58.730
Thanks to that, the crime rate in Shantytown
has been skyrocketing the past month.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.190
That's not good.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:03.570
Oh, wait, is that why Kozue is...

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:08.990
Apparently she's been wandering around
Shantytown lately, and so I followed her here.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.660
But you lost sight of her?

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:11.540
Well...

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.920
We gotta look for her.
You go on the north side!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.170
- S-Sure!
- Mr. Shindo? Yes.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:23.840
Drug D or not, Shantytown isn't a place where
Kozue should be wandering around by herself.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.850
Hazard Cast doesn't work here.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.720
<i>Hazard Cast automatically calculates
and predicts crime scenes</i>

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.770
<i>based on data collected within the city.</i>

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.110
<i>Shantytown, with so many old buildings,
has few surveillance cameras,</i>

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:41.610
<i>and cPhones with advanced sensors
can't be distributed to illegal immigrants.</i>

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:43.610
It's useless.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.820
<i>Just like a certain someone right now.</i>

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.490
<i>That's why this town needs redevelopment.</i>

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:53.620
<i>It needs monitoring with surveillance cameras,
and registration and management via cPhones.</i>

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.420
About that...

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:57.880
I feel like that's kinda scary.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.630
Like someone is watching over you at all times.
Doesn't that seem a bit constrained?

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.920
<i>That's a complaint
from the previous generation.</i>

00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:08.680
<i>Data sent from cPhones are encrypted
so personal information is under protection.</i>

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.520
<i>Is your heroism based on failing to notice
an incident that you can save</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.140
<i>because of a vague sense of uneasiness?</i>

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.890
Once again, someone dear to you—

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.400
<i>I get it!</i>

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.690
I get it.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:34.250
Hey.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:38.130
Are you looking for Drug D?

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:39.500
Huh? D?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:43.510
N-No, I'm not. I'm here for this.

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:54.930
Kozue, where did you go?

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.770
ASUMI

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:55.770
Shu!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.020
Long time no see!

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.060
Oh, Ran, it's been a while.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.530
But you're not the one
I'm looking for right now.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.530
You haven't had enough
with your hero activities?

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.610
No way. I'm just looking for Kozue.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.820
Kozue-chin?

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:10.530
I got separated from her.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.780
So dangerous.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:13.990
INFORMATION PLEASE
HAVE YOU SEEN THIS GIRL?

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:14.910
Hold on a sec. I'll ask my crew.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:16.710
Oh, Kunai's taking care of her.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:17.870
Kunai?

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.290
Someone from our super-brilliant crew.
You can relax now.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.960
Seriously? What a lifesaver.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.380
Geez, I'm so glad.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.630
Oh, I need to let Koki know.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.010
Hey, Kunai?

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:37.230
You haven't shown up at DoRed in a while.
Something up?

00:14:38.480 --> 00:14:41.270
<i>It's nothing. The same as always.</i>

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:46.360
I see. Well, if something's wrong,
you can contact me, okay?

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:48.820
Yeah. See ya.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.360
Shu.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.080
You came at a good time.
Can you come with me for a bit?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.290
So you were looking for graffiti?

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:03.960
I noticed the instant I saw it uploaded
on the internet, and thought, "Hey, this is Dad."

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:07.590
Everyone was calling him Kaba or Mr. Kaba.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:11.390
Besides, it's only been recently
that these pieces have started popping up

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.220
ever since the tornado during GourFes.

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:16.600
That's why you're in Shantytown?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.730
I want to know who drew them.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.730
Hey, would you happen to know?

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.110
DoRed's leader, Red.

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.280
You know?
Do you know where I can find them?

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:32.110
I can't tell you, even if I knew.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.320
Why?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.870
Do you know about the Wizard of Oz?

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:42.750
The wizard let his name spread across the land
by hiding his true identity.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.250
Well, I understand that I can't meet this person,

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:48.010
but can you tell me what kind of person Red is?

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:51.300
A genius artist.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.560
A child born in Shantytown
only has two futures to dream of.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:16:01.390
One is to become a criminal
and rule over the town with money,

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.650
and the other is to become an artist
and break away from this town.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:10.990
Red is the latter, and everyone expected him
to become an artist ever since he was young.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.740
His talent was so overwhelming,
everyone acknowledged it.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:18.040
But graffiti is a crime, right?

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:23.250
They say how Shantytown is dangerous
and needs redevelopment, right?

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.540
It's going to become a casino, right?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.500
Something about letting the government
control the area and make it safe.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:32.300
There are some fish
that can only live in murky waters.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:37.640
If they change the tank to clean water,
they no longer have a place to hide and get eaten.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:41.180
But nobody listens to the voices
of those living in the shadows.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.770
That can't be...

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:49.440
Red continues to draw graffiti on the streets
for all of us in Shantytown who're in that situation.

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.780
So he can change the world through art.

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.150
Change the world through art?

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:57.660
That's just not possible. I don't believe it.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:00.410
Red will do it someday.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:03.370
He's a genius artist, after all.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.170
<i>It's impossible for me, though.</i>

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:17.600
Here.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:20.100
Oh, thank you.

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.560
You do this every night?

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.190
Well, yeah.
But this is the last one of the series.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.270
What do you think about SuperKaba?

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.990
Kaba is a true hero.

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:42.040
You know, I've been scared ever since that day.

00:17:42.950 --> 00:17:45.920
What should I do if I have that Vision again?

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.080
I might end up
losing someone dear to me again.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.880
Why does it have to be me?

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.380
It'd be better to let someone else handle it.

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.300
We start meddling, and then screw up.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.140
And I feel like an idiot.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:10.270
The reason why Shantytown has a high crime rate
is the result of prejudice coinciding with data.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:16.110
The guys in SARG
calculate the crime rates from statistics.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:20.700
So if someone from Shantytown and someone
from another place are walking next to each other,

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.040
SARG will most definitely
approach us for questioning.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.620
And then they treat us like criminals.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:31.420
So Shantytown's crime rate goes up,
which leads to SARG intensifying their patrols.

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:35.590
You can say it's a chicken-or-the-egg question.

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:41.800
What creates crime isn't data,
but the hearts of people who look at the data.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:48.060
Even if you rely on Hazard Cast, that only fortifies
the rules of the world as it stands now.

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:52.400
If you want to change the world,
you have to change people's hearts.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:54.900
That's why...

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.990
I use this.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.370
That's so awesome.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:15.090
Change the world, huh?

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.300
Today's is so big.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:20.680
Kozue?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:24.220
I heard that a new art piece was here.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:26.140
Oh, I get it.

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.020
It's called SuperKaba.

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:30.940
So literal.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.520
Got a picture?

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.440
Yeah. See?

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.400
Looks good.

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.070
Wait, you have others?

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:44.240
Were you walking around
looking for the Kaba art?

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.280
Yeah.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:48.290
But why does he do things like this?

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.170
He puts in effort to draw these, but they
become meaningless when they get erased.

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.920
It's not meaningless.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.010
Even if it gets erased, it'll still remain.

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:00.050
Because I'll remember.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.640
I'll remember that someone drew this,
and that someone like this existed.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.690
So, how do I say it.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:18.610
Don't say stuff like
you should have died in his place.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.200
Then, Big Brother Shu.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.460
Can you protect me again?

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:37.420
Because Big Brother Shu...

00:20:39.260 --> 00:20:40.920
...you're my hero.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:45.930
Of course.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:53.810
Of course!
I'm one of Mr. Kaba's students.

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:56.940
Yup. You are.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:01.400
Want some rusk?

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:03.320
Yeah.

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.410
Yum.

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:08.080
We took our time baking with the rye.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:11.410
It's full of dietary fiber and minerals,
so it's got beauty benefits.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.750
Big Brother Shu, you really haven't changed.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.830
Come on now.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.130
What the...

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:19.710
It's just like a movie.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:21.210
What's that?

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.470
<i>Choose your future.</i>

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.930
<i>Choose your destiny.</i>

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:36.480
<i>Choose your future.</i>

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.610
That mark...

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:39.730
<i>Choose your destiny.</i>

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.860
Carneades.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:44.780
Big Brother Shu, isn't that the guy
who's rumored to have created the tornado?

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.160
Don't worry about it.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:49.030
All right, it looks like I can call out.

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:52.500
So this is a challenge from Carneades?

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.250
Still got quite a flashy performance.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:56.750
Both of you, listen up.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.170
Last time, we didn't have time
to talk it through.

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:01.300
But if all three of us worked together,

00:22:01.300 --> 00:22:03.460
I'm sure we would have ended up
with a different outcome.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.590
That sounds so like you, Shu.

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:09.850
But it was just a coincidence that we had
a third answer during that first bit with the Kizuna.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:15.310
Things might go towards the unexpected
just like last time. If we fail again...

00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:17.690
Still, I can't bear to abandon someone—

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:23.900
ASUMI

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:23.900
There it is. From Asumi.

00:22:24.740 --> 00:22:25.400
Ready?

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:26.780
- Yeah.
- Oui.

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:38.040
A luxurious cruise ship is sailing in Tokyo Bay.

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.500
VIPs are aboard that ship.

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:44.170
And terrorists have planted
a remote-control bomb on it.

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:46.920
There is only one way to stop the crime.

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:52.140
Will you snipe the perpetrator and kill him
to stop the ship from exploding?

00:22:53.010 --> 00:22:54.600
Or will you let the perpetrator go...

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:04.230
and allow many people to die
from the exploding ship?

00:23:05.480 --> 00:23:07.990
Guide the future.

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.160
Another trolley dilemma.

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:18.080
There's no room for debate.

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:21.630
I can't abandon innocent victims
and succumb to terrorism.

00:23:21.630 --> 00:23:24.040
But this isn't really two choices.

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.920
Are you saying this is a trick question?

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.840
The terrorist who was shot dead.

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:30.550
That was...

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:32.680
Kunai.

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:38.680
A child born in Shantytown
only has two futures to dream of.

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:42.940
One is to become a criminal
and rule over the town with money,

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:46.690
and the other is to become an artist
and break away from this town.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:51.360
As someone with no talent as an artist,

00:23:58.040 --> 00:23:59.370
I...
